# pennyos: earlyoom closes the biggest app before low memory freezes the desktop
# (the kernel's own OOM killer only acts after a long stall). It acts once available
# memory is under 15 % AND free swap is under 10 %: only when zram is full and the swap
# file on the eMMC is nearly full too. The memory figure is high because, once swap is
# full, MemAvailable still counts several hundred MB that cannot really be freed.
# --avoid: the session itself (compositor, login, bar, radio, ssh); losing one of
# these loses the desktop. --prefer: voice typing, which restarts on the next use.
# No quotes around the patterns: systemd splits these arguments at spaces only.
EARLYOOM_ARGS="-m 15 -s 10 -r 3600 --avoid ^(niri|greetd|gtkgreet|systemd.*|sshd|dbus-.*|waybar|penny-.*|wpa_supplicant)$ --prefer ^whisper-cli$"
